    "title": "2026 Oscar Nominations: See the Full List",
    "text": "AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENTYou have been granted access, use your keyboard to continue reading.The movies competing for the 98th Academy Awards. The ceremony will air on March 15.Teyana Taylor in “One Battle After Another,” which received 13 Oscar nominations.Credit...Warner Bros.Jan. 22, 2026The nominations for the 98th Academy Awards were announced Thursday morning. Leading the pack was “Sinners,” with a record-breaking 16 nominations, including best picture, best director for Ryan Coogler and best actor for Michael B. Jordan. “One Battle After Another” received one nomination after another for a total of 13, also including best picture, best director for Paul Thomas Anderson and best actor for Leonardo DiCaprio.Timothée Chalamet is in the running for best actor as well for “Marty Supreme,” which would make him one of the youngest best actor winners after Adrien Brody’s win for “The Pianist” in 2003. Also notable in the acting categories is “Sentimental Value,” with its entire main cast getting nods at four nominations: Renate Reinsve for best actress, Stellan Skarsgard for best supporting actor, and both Elle Fanning and Inga Ibsdotter Lilleaas for best supporting actress.The ceremony will take place on March 15 and Conan O’Brien will be returning as the host. Below is the full list of nominees.Best PictureImageTimothée Chalamet was nominated for his performance in “Marty Supreme,” which also received nominations in the directing and best picture categories.Credit...A24Best DirectorPaul Thomas Anderson, “One Battle After Another”Josh Safdie, “Marty Supreme”Joachim Trier, “Sentimental Value”Chloé Zhao, “Hamnet”Best ActorTimothée Chalamet, “Marty Supreme”Ethan Hawke, “Blue Moon”Michael B. Jordan, “Sinners”Wagner Moura, “The Secret Agent”ImageJessie Buckley, center, received a nomination for her role in “Hamnet.”Credit...Agata Grzybowska/Focus FeaturesBest ActressJessie Buckley, “Hamnet”Rose Byrne, “If I Had Legs I’d Kick You”Kate Hudson, “Song Sung Blue”Renate Reinsve, “Sentimental Value”Emma Stone, “Bugonia”Best Supporting ActorJacob Elordi, “Frankenstein”Delroy Lindo, “Sinners”Stellan Skarsgard, “Sentimental Value”Best Supporting ActressElle Fanning, “Sentimental Value”Inga Ibsdotter Lilleaas, “Sentimental Value”Teyana Taylor, “One Battle After Another”Original Screenplay“Blue Moon”“It Was Just an Accident”“Marty Supreme”“Sentimental Value”“Sinners”ImageMichael B. Jordan, left and center, was nominated for “Sinners.”Credit...Warner Bros.Adapted Screenplay“Bugonia”“Frankenstein”“Hamnet”“One Battle After Another”“Train Dreams”Casting“Hamnet”“Marty Supreme”“One Battle After Another”“Sinners”“The Secret Agent”Editing“F1”“Marty Supreme”“One Battle After Another”“Sentimental Value”“Sinners”ImageJavier Bardem, left, with Brad Pitt in “F1,” which was nominated for best picture.Credit...Scott Garfield/Warner Bros. and AppleAnimated FeatureDocumentary FeatureInternational FeatureImageFrom left, Stefania Gadda, Joshua Liam Herderson, Richard Bellamy and Sergi López in a scene from the film “Sirat,” nominated in the international feature category.Credit...NeonProduction Design“Frankenstein”“Hamnet”“Marty Supreme”“One Battle After Another”“Sinners”Costume Design“Avatar: Fire and Ash”“Frankenstein”“Hamnet”“Marty Supreme”“Sinners”Cinematography“Frankenstein”“Marty Supreme”“One Battle After Another”“Sinners”“Train Dreams”Makeup and Hairstyling“Frankenstein”“Kokuho”“Sinners”“The Smashing Machine”“The Ugly Stepsister”ImageJacob Elordi was nominated for his role in “Frankenstein.”Credit...NetflixSound“F1”“Frankenstein”“One Battle After Another”“Sinners”“Sirat”Visual Effects“Avatar: Fire and Ash”“F1”“Jurassic World Rebirth”“The Lost Bus”“Sinners”Original Score“Bugonia”“Frankenstein”“Hamnet”“One Battle After Another”“Sinners”ImageEmma Stone received an acting nomination for “Bugonia.”Credit...Atsushi Nishijima/Focus FeaturesOriginal Song“Dear Me” (“Diane Warren: Relentless”)“Golden” (“KPop Demon Hunters”)“I Lied to You” (“Sinners”)“Sweet Dreams of Joy” (“Viva Verdi!”)“Train Dreams” (“Train Dreams”)Animated Short“Butterfly”“Forevergreen”“The Girl Who Cried Pearls”“Retirement Plan”“The Three Sisters”Documentary Short“All the Empty Rooms”“Armed Only With a Camera: The Life and Death of Brent Renaud”“Children No More: “Were and Are Gone”“The Devil Is Busy”“Perfectly a Strangeness”Live-Action Short“Butcher’s Stain”“A Friend of Dorothy”“Jane Austen’s Period Drama”“The Singers”“Two People Exchanging Saliva”Shivani Gonzalez is a news assistant at The Times who writes a weekly TV column and contributes to a variety of sections.A version of this article appears in print on Jan. 23, 2026, Section C, Page 7 of the New York edition with the headline: Nominees for the Academy Awards. Order Reprints | Today’s Paper | SubscribeRelated ContentAdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENT",
